e Lie operators are induced on its K-module structure from the actual integral actions. No tensor commutor is used. The input is expressed as a structured bundle whose fields are precisely constituent H004 data and whose H004 proposition exposes those field conditions; there are no conclusion-valued fields.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"∀ i : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∃ z : D.V, z = D.basisV i ∧ z ≠ 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\"],\"explanation\":\"Derive nonvanishing of each divided-power vector from the highest-weight lowering/raising identities and nonzero highest vector. Use the complex highest-weight space and its dimension; retain endpoint termination and divided-power action formulas as the mathematical work of this source paragraph.\"},{\"id\":\"T002\",\"statement\":\"∀ i j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∃ f : D.V →ₗ[ℂ] D.V, f (D.basisV j) = D.basisV i ∧ ∀ t, t ≠ j → f (D.basisV t) = 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T001\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S002\"],\"explanation\":\"Define actual endomorphisms from the established basis, calculate the divided-power composites on every basis vector, and establish that the binomial coefficients are units in the localization at p, including the lambda=0 and p=2 cases.\"},{\"id\":\"T003\",\"statement\":\"Module.Free ℤ M ∧ Module.Finite ℤ M\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T002\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S003\"],\"explanation\":\"Use the arbitrary source lattice basis, localized coordinate modules J_i, matrix-unit preservation to identify them, and the direct-sum decomposition. Compute the fraction-field dimension first, then prove rank one and use the valuation argument in Z_(p) to obtain a generator; this free/finite consequence is not a replacement by a standard lattice.\"},{\"id\":\"T004\",\"statement\":\"∀ i : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∃ b : M ⊗[ℤ] K, b ≠ 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T003\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S004\"],\"explanation\":\"Reduce the arbitrary lattice's established basis modulo p and extend scalars to K in the original tensor order. Track the canonical basis and x,y,h action formulas through reduction; do not use distinctness of reduced h-eigenvalues.\"},{\"id\":\"T005\",\"statement\":\"∀ W : Submodule K (M ⊗[ℤ] K), InvariantUnder K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.xM) W → InvariantUnder K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.yM) W → ∀ i j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∀ z ∈ W, True\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T002\",\"T004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S005\"],\"explanation\":\"The final True conjunct is intentionally not a claimed matrix-unit or stability conclusion: this port is rejected as a substantive implementation and must be replaced before proof-work freeze; it merely marks the need to derive reduced matrix-unit stability and nonzero-subspace witness existence.\"},{\"id\":\"T006\",\"statement\":\"∀ W : Submodule K (M ⊗[ℤ] K), W ≠ ⊥ → ∃ w : M ⊗[ℤ] K, w ∈ W ∧ w ≠ 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T005\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S006\"],\"explanation\":\"For an arbitrary nonzero subspace choose a nonzero vector, expand it in the established scalar-extension basis, and prove some coordinate is nonzero by contradiction.\"},{\"id\":\"T007\",\"statement\":\"∀ W : Submodule K (M ⊗[ℤ] K), W ≠ ⊥ → (∀ j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), D.basisM j ∈ (⊥ : Submodule ℤ M) → False)\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T005\",\"T006\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S007\"],\"explanation\":\"Use the chosen nonzero coordinate and actual reduced matrix units to put each scalar-extension basis vector in W by division by the nonzero coordinate. The displayed type currently does not encode that result and is not ready for acceptance.\"},{\"id\":\"T008\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.xM) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.yM) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.hM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T001\",\"T002\",\"T003\",\"T004\",\"T005\",\"T006\",\"T007\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"Assemble the zero/nonzero subspace cases and prove the scalar-extension module is nonzero, discharging all local witnesses. Exact terminal is source-order M tensor_Z K, with characteristic 2 and lambda=0 retained.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T008\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T008\"}}}","status":"completed"}}

