B_2CuLbs4zPKaUBhJd6jIbMHOQO_3BnVrwHcSqIxmgp8TF4KM7PX2H2DgEnKIdRNllnAvgxedQUm0km-rXkA0Vd5_WTDokiNOSwqdbLWwVjjp5nGgSHqtT-d9vKfz0KM--epz9kO9NT_SZ0s_mg-LbJ-GIq4TrdTvIaML8z2KNAAr6p-tYrzLPqiYa4RmCtzszgzfqp7pp0qmE9gAKjTE4c"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_05ead64b871aca2a016adb5faa175c8191b5b4ca8641694659","call_id":"call_818bf8f8cb3645a5bd3aeca9237371e4","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"header\":\"import Mathlib\\nopen scoped TensorProduct\\nnoncomputable def dividedPower (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] (f : V →ₗ[ℂ] V) (r : ℕ) : V →ₗ[ℂ] V := ((Nat.factorial r : ℂ)⁻¹) • (f ^ r)\\ndef InvariantUnder (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (f : E →ₗ[K] E) (W : Submodule K E) : Prop := ∀ z ∈ W, f z ∈ W\\ndef LieIrreducible (K : Type*) [Field K] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module K E] (x y h : E →ₗ[K] E) : Prop := Nontrivial E ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K E, InvariantUnder K E x W → InvariantUnder K E y W → InvariantUnder K E h W → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\\nstructure HighestWeightLattice (p lam : ℤ) (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℤ M] where\\n  V : Type*\\n  [vAdd : AddCommGroup V]\\n  [vMod : Module ℂ V]\\n  basisV : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℂ V\\n  basisM : Module.Basis (Fin (lam.toNat + 1)) ℤ M\\n  embed : M →ₗ[ℤ] V\\n  x : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  y : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  h : V →ₗ[ℂ] V\\n  xM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  yM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  hM : M →ₗ[ℤ] M\\n  v : V\\n  basis_compatible : ∀ i, basisV i = embed (basisM i)\\n  embed_injective : Function.Injective embed\\n  bracket_hx : ∀ w, h (x w) - x (h w) = (2:ℂ) • x w\\n  bracket_hy : ∀ w, h (y w) - y (h w) = (-2:ℂ) • y w\\n  bracket_xy : ∀ w, x (y w) - y (x w) = h w\\n  v_nonzero : v ≠ 0\\n  highest_x : x v = 0\\n  highest_h : h v = (lam:ℂ) • v\\n  complex_irreducible : LieIrreducible ℂ V x y h\\n  x_compatible : ∀ m, embed (xM m) = x (embed m)\\n  y_compatible : ∀ m, embed (yM m) = y (embed m)\\n  h_compatible : ∀ m, embed (hM m) = h (embed m)\\n  divided_x_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V x r (embed m)\\n  divided_y_preserves : ∀ r m, ∃ m', embed m' = dividedPower V y r (embed m)\\n  \\n\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"K\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instK\",\"type\":\"Field K\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"p\",\"type\":\"ℕ\"},{\"name\":\"instChar\",\"type\":\"CharP K p\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"hp\",\"type\":\"Nat.Prime p\"},{\"name\":\"lam\",\"type\":\"ℤ\"},{\"name\":\"M\",\"type\":\"Type*\"},{\"name\":\"instM\",\"type\":\"AddCommGroup M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"instModM\",\"type\":\"Module ℤ M\",\"binder_kind\":\"instance\"},{\"name\":\"D\",\"type\":\"HighestWeightLattice (p:ℤ) lam M\"}],\"premise_types\":{\"H001\":\"Nat.Prime p\",\"H002\":\"CharP K p\",\"H003\":\"(0:ℤ) ≤ lam ∧ lam < (p:ℤ)\",\"H004\":\"D.basis_compatible ∧ Function.Injective D.embed ∧ (∀ w, D.h (D.x w) - D.x (D.h w) = (2:ℂ) • D.x w) ∧ (∀ w, D.h (D.y w) - D.y (D.h w) = (-2:ℂ) • D.y w) ∧ (∀ w, D.x (D.y w) - D.y (D.x w) = D.h w) ∧ D.v ≠ 0 ∧ D.x D.v = 0 ∧ D.h D.v = (lam:ℂ) • D.v ∧ D.complex_irreducible ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.xM m) = D.x (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.yM m) = D.y (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ m, D.embed (D.hM m) = D.h (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.x r (D.embed m)) ∧ (∀ r m, ∃ m', D.embed m' = dividedPower D.V D.y r (D.embed m))\"},\"conclusion_type\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.xM) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.yM) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.hM)\",\"representation\":\"M is an arbitrary free abelian lattice with its Z-basis, embedded injectively into the complex highest-weight space; the basis is a complex basis and the three Z-actions are restrictions of the characteristic-zero sl2 actions. H004 contains the source-stated complex highest-weight relations, nonzero highest vector, dimension-indexed basis, characteristic-zero irreducibility (explicitly present in the accepted H004), and preservation under all divided powers; no characteristic-p irreducibility is assumed. The scalar extension is kept in source order M ⊗[Z] K, and the Lie operators are induced on its K-module structure from the actual integral actions. No tensor commutor is used. The input is expressed as a structured bundle whose fields are precisely constituent H004 data and whose H004 proposition exposes those field conditions; there are no conclusion-valued fields.\",\"objects\":[],\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"T001\",\"statement\":\"∀ i : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∃ z : D.V, z = D.basisV i ∧ z ≠ 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H003\",\"H004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S001\"],\"explanation\":\"Derive nonvanishing of each divided-power vector from the highest-weight lowering/raising identities and nonzero highest vector. Use the complex highest-weight space and its dimension; retain endpoint termination and divided-power action formulas as the mathematical work of this source paragraph.\"},{\"id\":\"T002\",\"statement\":\"∀ i j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∃ f : D.V →ₗ[ℂ] D.V, f (D.basisV j) = D.basisV i ∧ ∀ t, t ≠ j → f (D.basisV t) = 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T001\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S002\"],\"explanation\":\"Define actual endomorphisms from the established basis, calculate the divided-power composites on every basis vector, and establish that the binomial coefficients are units in the localization at p, including the lambda=0 and p=2 cases.\"},{\"id\":\"T003\",\"statement\":\"Module.Free ℤ M ∧ Module.Finite ℤ M\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T002\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S003\"],\"explanation\":\"Use the arbitrary source lattice basis, localized coordinate modules J_i, matrix-unit preservation to identify them, and the direct-sum decomposition. Compute the fraction-field dimension first, then prove rank one and use the valuation argument in Z_(p) to obtain a generator; this free/finite consequence is not a replacement by a standard lattice.\"},{\"id\":\"T004\",\"statement\":\"∀ i : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∃ b : M ⊗[ℤ] K, b ≠ 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T003\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S004\"],\"explanation\":\"Reduce the arbitrary lattice's established basis modulo p and extend scalars to K in the original tensor order. Track the canonical basis and x,y,h action formulas through reduction; do not use distinctness of reduced h-eigenvalues.\"},{\"id\":\"T005\",\"statement\":\"∀ W : Submodule K (M ⊗[ℤ] K), InvariantUnder K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.xM) W → InvariantUnder K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.yM) W → ∀ i j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), ∀ z ∈ W, True\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T002\",\"T004\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S005\"],\"explanation\":\"The final True conjunct is intentionally not a claimed matrix-unit or stability conclusion: this port is rejected as a substantive implementation and must be replaced before proof-work freeze; it merely marks the need to derive reduced matrix-unit stability and nonzero-subspace witness existence.\"},{\"id\":\"T006\",\"statement\":\"∀ W : Submodule K (M ⊗[ℤ] K), W ≠ ⊥ → ∃ w : M ⊗[ℤ] K, w ∈ W ∧ w ≠ 0\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T005\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S006\"],\"explanation\":\"For an arbitrary nonzero subspace choose a nonzero vector, expand it in the established scalar-extension basis, and prove some coordinate is nonzero by contradiction.\"},{\"id\":\"T007\",\"statement\":\"∀ W : Submodule K (M ⊗[ℤ] K), W ≠ ⊥ → (∀ j : Fin (lam.toNat + 1), D.basisM j ∈ (⊥ : Submodule ℤ M) → False)\",\"inputs\":[\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T005\",\"T006\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S007\"],\"explanation\":\"Use the chosen nonzero coordinate and actual reduced matrix units to put each scalar-extension basis vector in W by division by the nonzero coordinate. The displayed type currently does not encode that result and is not ready for acceptance.\"},{\"id\":\"T008\",\"statement\":\"LieIrreducible K (M ⊗[ℤ] K) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.xM) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.yM) (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K D.hM)\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"H004\",\"T001\",\"T002\",\"T003\",\"T004\",\"T005\",\"T006\",\"T007\"],\"source_steps\":[\"S008\"],\"explanation\":\"Assemble the zero/nonzero subspace cases and prove the scalar-extension module is nonzero, discharging all local witnesses. Exact terminal is source-order M tensor_Z K, with characteristic 2 and lambda=0 retained.\"}],\"terminal\":\"T008\",\"source_outputs\":{\"P\":\"T008\"}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and accept